ideline references 201/202/203/210/211 + REACH 1907/2006 attributed correctly per p. 21; no invented LODs/instruments/reference materials. Check 4 Part 12 brand firewall ✅: zero commercial detergent brand names; only EU Ecolabel programme mark (permitted), regulatory/standards bodies (EC/JRC/ECHA/ATCC/EFSA/EUCAST/RSPO/IDA/OECD/ISO), CAS-identified substances (EDTA/DTPA/atranol/chloroatranol/glutaraldehyde/HICC/MIT/BIT/CMIT-MIT/triclosan/IPBC/Rhodamine-B/formaldehyde-releasers permitted as scientific identifiers), OECD/ISO test-method numbers (Exception 2). Check 5 Part 2 wiki/HMTc firewall ✅: no HMTc threshold proposals (Implications section explicitly states none proposed); no consumer-audience risk advisories; the User-Manual-vs-TR2-deck mercury-naming contrast is faithful within-source-family description not cross-literature synthesis; missing-slug observations properly housed in Verification notes. Routing unchanged (10 product rows direct_evidence + advisory-only malformed for empty ingredients/matrices consistent with sibling EU Ecolabel pages ral2024, jrc2025, eeb2022). No audit-application commit (PROMOTE with no content changes per skill Phase 3 step 13)."
